{"id":4456,"date":"2025-02-25T06:16:06","date_gmt":"2025-02-25T06:16:06","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/?post_type=projects&#038;p=4456"},"modified":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","modified_gmt":"2025-04-16T00:36:54","slug":"hc-kim-reserve-pavilion","status":"publish","type":"projects","link":"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/project\/hc-kim-reserve-pavilion\/","title":{"rendered":"HC Kim Reserve Pavilion"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-info\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div class=\"grid__details\"\">\n\n                \n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Location<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Millers Road, Seaholme<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Client name<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Hobsons Bay City Council\/Loaram Constructions<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Value<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>$4.7 MIL<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Timeframe<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>2021-2024<\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Contractor<\/h5>\n                            <p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/loaram.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Loaram Constructions<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                        <div>\n                            <h5>Consultant Team<\/h5>\n                            <p><p>Structural &amp; Civil Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.adamseng.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Adams Consulting Engineer<\/a><br \/>\nServices Engineer &#8211; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.njmdesign.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NJM Design<\/a><br \/>\nQuantity Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"http:\/\/www.prowseqs.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prowse Quantity Surveyors<\/a><br \/>\nBuilding Surveyor &#8211; <a href=\"https:\/\/www.bwanational.com.au\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BW&amp;A National Building Consultants<\/a><\/p>\n<\/p>\n                        <\/div>\n\n                    \n                \n                \n                \n                                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__text\">\n                <p>This thoughtfully designed single-storey community pavilion at HC Kim Reserve in Seaholme serves as a modern hub for both local residents and visitors. The pavilion is strategically planned to accommodate a wide range of activities and foster community engagement.<\/p>\n<p>The facility includes six spacious changerooms, providing separate spaces for both male and female participants, ensuring comfort and privacy. Central to the building is a Social Room, designed as a versatile space for gatherings, meetings, and community events. Large windows offer views of the surrounding reserve, creating a welcoming atmosphere for all who enter.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0066-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0066-1.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0066-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0066-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0066-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate block-quote\">\n        <div class=\"max-sm:w-full ml-auto w-1\/2\">\n            <div>\n                <blockquote>\n\n                <p>HC Kim Reserve Pavilion stands out for its large, flexible function room which overlooks the sports field, providing plenty of room for spectators to watch and support their team play soccer.<\/p>\n\n                \n                <\/blockquote>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-thirds-image\">\n        <div class=\"grid\">\n            <div>\n                            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate two-columns-text-image\">\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        <div class=\"grid mt-[30px] md:mt-[50px]\">\n\n            <div class=\"grid__text space-y-12\">\n                                <div><p>An outdoor viewing area offers a central vantage point for spectators, making it ideal for enjoying local sporting events and recreational activities. The design emphasizes seamless indoor-outdoor flow, fostering a sense of openness and connection to the natural environment.<\/p>\n<p>This pavilion not only enhances the functionality of HC Kim Reserve but also contributes to the overall sense of community by providing a space for social interaction, sports, and recreation in the heart of Seaholme.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n                            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"grid__image\">\n                 <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"620\" height=\"744\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0175-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0175-1.jpg 620w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0175-1-250x300.jpg 250w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 620px) 100vw, 620px\" \/>            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate full-width-image\">\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1320\" height=\"880\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0017-1.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0017-1.jpg 1320w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0017-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0017-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0017-1-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px\" \/>    <\/section>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    <section class=\"block block-animate project-carousel\">\n\n        <div class=\"swiper swiper-block\">\n\n            \n                <div class=\"swiper-wrapper\">\n                    \n                                        \n                        <div class=\"swiper-slide\">\n                            <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"962\" height=\"641\" src=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0051.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0051.jpg 962w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0051-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/architecturematters.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/43A0051-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 962px) 100vw, 962px\" \/>                        <\/div>\n\n                           